					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-25 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br>What a beautiful day of weather this Sunday. Too bad I decided to go record digging instead of mowing the lawn.<br /><br />I&#39;m still on a high from last Friday&#39;s Stop the Killings benefit concert - the show was a success and definitely a collaborative effort put in by everyone. Some fam from Portland drove up to Seattle to see it...even our kasama Helene flew in from the Bay (or is it LA now haha). Peep the photos below (courtesy of Mike Antonio and Sonia Abenojar)!<br /><br />And just today, the Permanent People&#39;s Tribunal has found Philippine President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo and her administration responsible for the many solved murders and disappearances in the Philippines. Peep out the article <a href="http://newsinfo.inquirer.net/inquirerheadlines/nation/view_article.php?article_id=56941">here</a>.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/169/433373993_b40f5cda1b.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Lovework courtesy of the Native Gunner, Kiwi.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/188/433375737_9e699125b8.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />El Dia rocks the mic while i push the buttons.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/176/433375654_a714bbb41f.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Fierce energy also courtesy of Kiwi.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/164/433380253_bd39523b41.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Geo breaks it down.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/177/433377790_3b815b14a5.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Sabzi cameo in the last act of the final chapter. <br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/152/433379256_8f7c6a8da3.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Check out that&#39;s youth&#39;s thizz face. Lovin&#39; it.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/169/433373911_651a00951a.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Fin.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-23 | Friday</font></strong><br><br><img src="file:///C:/DOCUME%7E1/ADMINI%7E1/LOCALS%7E1/Temp/moz-screenshot.jpg" alt="" /><br />The excitement is at its <strong>zenith</strong> right now cuz today is the day to make history. The build up from the Stop the Killings tour comes to a <strong>climax</strong> tonight as Prometheus Brown (Geologic&#39;s superhero alter ego) headlines the Seattle (and final?) STK show. For more information, <a href="../smf/index.php?topic=1385.0">check this ish out</a>.  <br /><br />But before that, check out your boys Blue Scholars as they head up north(east) to rock the <strong><em>hell</em></strong> out of Bothell:<br /><br />Friday, March 23, 7:30 pm Doors<br />$18 Adult / $15 Student<br />All Ages<br />Northshore Performing Arts Center<br />18125 92nd Ave. NE, Bothell<br />Tickets at <a href="http://www.ticketswest.com/" target="_blank">www.TicketsWest.com</a><br />more info at <a href="http://www.npacf.org/" target="_blank">www.npacf.org</a><br /><br />Quick random shoutouts: Sabzi&#39;s haircut, WAPIFASA, peekaboo!, Shorewood HS, and your mom.<br /><br />Peace<br />dj daps1<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-22 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>Here it is. The hype and the hate has begun (read <a href="http://www.thestranger.com/seattle/Content?oid=180349">The<br />Stranger</a> lately?). Peace to<strong> Peekaboo</strong> (who designed the most recent Blue Scholars Limited Edition Tee - sold out!) for designing the album artwork for <strong>Bayani</strong>.
Again, the new album will be available exclusively at Blue Scholars
shows beginning May 11 (&amp; 12th - at our Bayani album release
parties - info in the column on the right) and in stores nationwide on <strong>June 12</strong>!<br /><br />We&#39;ve posted two tracks off the album (<em>North by Northwest</em> &amp; <em>Back Home</em>) at our <a href="http://www.myspace.com/bluescholars"> MYSPACE.COM/BLUESCHOLARS</a> page.<br /><br />Aaaaand... here&#39;s the final tracklsting:<br /><br />1. Baha&#39;i Healing Prayer (intro)<br />2. Second Chapter<br />3. Opening Salvo<br />4. North by Northwest<br />5. Ordinary Guy<br />6. Still Got Love<br />7. Bayani<br />8. Loyalty<br />9. Fire for the People<br />10. Xenophobia (interlude)<br />11. The Distance<br />12. Back Home<br />13. 50 Thousand Deep<br />14. Morning of America<br />15. Joe Metro<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-22 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>yesterday was <strong>Naw Ruz</strong> people!<br /><br /><strong>&quot;Eid-e shoma mobarak!  Sol-e-noh mobarak!&quot;<br /></strong><br />this explicative and others were heard and used all day and night yesterday by<strong> Iranians</strong> and <strong>Baha&#39;is</strong> the world over.  although two very distinct communities, they share the same date for the New Year.<br /><br />in other news, the sun came back to Seattle, or so we thought.<br /><br /><u><strong>get your gear, get laced up</strong></u><br /><br />if you ain&#39;t already knowin, there&#39;s a new shop in town to cop all your fresh gear including Alife, Artful Dodger, Greedy Genius, and more.  last friday, before the PUSH MC battle you might have caught some of your townmates attending the <strong>Laced Up</strong> launch party on Cap Hill.  i was there with <strong>Larry Mizell</strong>, <strong>Darvin Vida (Boohi/PFOM)</strong>, <strong>Rik Rude</strong>, <strong>Bean One</strong>, <strong>Lord Vintage</strong>, and a number of the town&#39;s other urban elite.  just bein in the crowd made me feel too cool for school cuzzo.<br /><br /><img src="http://myspace-992.vo.llnwd.net/01586/29/97/1586507992_m.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />you see, the Seattle heads are coming to realize that the bland styles available at your local department stores just <em>aren&#39;t cutting it for the folks who need their fresh to be respected</em>.  that&#39;s why i had to stop in and congratulate my new friends <strong>Cassius</strong> and <strong>Kemetik</strong> on the new venture and thank them for puttin in work to develop the local culture of our humble town.<br /><br />checkem out!<br /><br /><a href="http://www.myspace.com/getlacedup"><strong>Laced Up</strong></a><br />705A East Pike St <br />Seattle, WA 98122<br /><br />oh yea, the artwork on the walls is pretty filthy too.<br /><br />Saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-20 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><p><strong>Greetings, humans!</strong>&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Massline</strong> emcee extraordinaire <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong>
and <strong>I</strong> performed at <strong>Westlake Cente</strong>r in downtown Seattle, yesterday
March 19, amidst a mixture of youth, veterans, media and community organizers
to protest the illegal war in Iraq. It was good to see a lot of youth close to
the stage, with one guy in particular yelling &quot;<em>that&#39;s bullshit!</em>&quot; every
20 minutes. I think that should be the new phrase&hellip;so feel free to say it while
other people are talking about imperialism, racism, classism, Hurricane Katrina,
Snickers commercials, all-over print hoodies, 835+ murders in the Philippines,
41 cent postal stamps, 50 Cent, Bryant and Greg Gumbel, Bill Buckner, blood
diamonds and hidden bank fees, amongst other things.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Anyway, Gabe and I were interviewed by the <strong>Seattle Times</strong>
but didn&#39;t make the article, nor did we make it on TV (to my knowledge). Wassup
with that? We&#39;re looking for our big break&hellip;it&#39;s also so I can afford a watch to
keep track of how many minutes of fame I&#39;ve already used up. Big ups to the <strong>Troops
Home Now Coalition</strong> for holding down Westlake and for having inspiring high
school youth up there offer their thoughts with enthusiasm. </p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>I, like you (yes you) should be enthused about this Friday&#39;s
<strong>Stop the Killings</strong> show at the newly built <strong>Vera Project</strong> in Seattle
Center. Your boy <strong>Prometheus Brown</strong> will headline, with <strong>Kiwi</strong> of the
<strong>Native Guns</strong> as one of the many guest performers. The show is going to offer
a whole lot more, so come through and show your support&hellip;it&#39;s needed now more
than ever. Check out the Massline forums for the info!</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Peace<br /><span style="font-size: 12pt">dj daps1</span></p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> [39] <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?